&gt; As for the Latin mass, yes it was there, and if you wanted to know what was said then you could always find out<p>Latin prayer books usually have the translation side by side. Attendants of the traditional Mass find value in it - it&#x27;s <i>truly</i> Catholic since you take part into it like anybody else worldwide, praying the same prayers, regardless of your native language, that have been prayed over the last ~5 centuries, some of which are 10, 15 or almost 20 centuries old.<p>&lt;conspiracy_theory&gt; The Vatican Council II&#x27;s original purpose wasn&#x27;t in fact to abolish the traditional Mass, but to help with increasingly difficult evangelization. What happened was instead largely due to the worldwide infiltration of the Church by the freemasons. &lt;&#x2F;conspiracy_theory&gt;<p>&lt;reality_check&gt;
Pope John Paul I publicly declared upon being elected, that he&#x27;d expose and get rid of them - freemasons weren&#x27;t in fact allowed as members the Church - priests, bishops, cardinals - and have never been, since they are obviously against the Church, but he knew they were there still.<p>On the evening before he died, the Pope received Pecorelli, a journalist that was a member of the masonic P2 lodge, who famously gave him a list of Catholic bishops and cardinals that were members of the freemasonry.<p>The Pope died a few hours after reading his list, his death never really investigated. The list disappeared; Pecorelli died a few months later in a car accident.<p>The P2 lodge was involved in other scandals, and as a consequence, some of its then members&#x27; names were exposed, and are now public - including some of the most powerful Italian politicians, entrepreneurs etc. of the time; now, after four decades, most of them are dead anyway - everything else is history.<p>Freemasonry in Italy came well before they entered the Vatican though - it&#x27;s not even too far fetched to think that Italy itself was created by them - Garibaldi was the founder of the main Italian FM branch, of which he became the Grand Master (with the &quot;33th degree&quot;) - the Grande Oriente d&#x27;Italia. Mazzini and other famous &quot;fathers of the country&quot; were also freemasons as well.<p>Ironically, Freemasonry - probably the most powerful, concealed, deceiving cult in the world - has not even a minor mention in this list. &lt;sad &#x2F;&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;reality_check&gt;<p>You can read about all of this on Wikipedia and elsewhere.
